Z||000054||FieroMontreal||12-05-2001||10:35 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Tabs31:<BR><B>Speed Zone!!!! kicked butt!!!! don't know there year that it came out.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>You bet it did.. the movie came out in 1989. Great cast and great cars. I watch that movie every once in a while.. I love that movie.. I've been watching it since I was a young boy.. Spent hundreds of dollars renting the movie over the years.. Finally found my own copy.. Did you notice the Fiero? It's being pulled over by the cops... Jason and Alexander are phoneing in stolen cars and they report a stolen Red Fiero.. then you see the car being stoped by the cops.. It's a Mera I think!!<P><P>------------------<BR> -Alex <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigfieromontreal_1.gif">   <BR>1986 Fiero GT, STOCK Wingless, <BR>President of FieroMontreal... <A HREF="http://www.fieromontreal.com" TARGET=_blank>www.fieromontreal.com</A> <BR>and Regional Director of CFOG-I for Eastern Canada.||||reg||1
Z||000055||Old Lar||12-05-2001||10:55 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by DR650SE:<BR><B>Isn't Bullit the movie where in the car chase seen the car looses 5 hubcaps?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Best chase scene movie.. I think it started the car chase theme.  The many hub caps that kept flying. plus the same VW gets passed twice because the same stretch of street was filmed from two directions.  I got to see that move while I was in Vietnam, Egad was it that long ago?<P>Christine is a real good one..I have it on DVD now. Mad, Mad, Mad World has a lot of car scenes in it.  That was made 1959-60 with so many stars in cameo performances as well as the stars.  One of the real funny movies.<BR>||||reg||1
