Z||000058||GTFiero1||12-06-2001||10:32 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Rex:<BR><B>Put me down for Vanishing Point<BR>The motorcycle scene was.........nice<BR>also. Was'nt that challenger a hemi?<BR>I got a rockin,rollin,realin.fellin.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>ya and is was an experimental twin turbo one that he had to deliver<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 84fierotrevor:<BR>[B] obvisily u havn't seen some of those car's.<BR>I got a video of a mustang saleen lossing to a supra. B]<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>...oh wow, thats surprising...<P>------------------<BR>Adam J. B.<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fiero_3.jpg">   <BR>you gotta keep on keepin on...<BR>IM AOL: GTFiero &  Rumpdetective (dont ask)||||reg||1
Z||000059||Raydar||12-07-2001||12:51 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by California Kid:<BR><B>"Up In Smoke"<BR>LMAO   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Yup. Forgot about that one. I liked the VeeDub with the pirated Rolls radiator shell.<P>Cannonball Run. <BR>Much of it was filmed in Decatur, GA. The 7-11, where Sammy Davis and Dean Martin had their argument, was walking distance from my house. The Cannonball Pub was actually the Olde English Inn, about 1.5 miles from home. We went up and watched them film.  <BR>Didn't get to meet anybody special, but saw some really awesome cars. Brock Yates produced it. It was more authentic than the others.<P>Gone in 60 Seconds (original) was the best chase scene I've ever seen.<P>Dirty Mary and Crazy Larry was pretty good. Starred Peter Fonda. <BR>Similar to Vanishing Point, except it took place in the walnut groves in Fla(?). The *star* was a yellow 69 or 70 Charger.<BR>Similar bummer ending. <P><P>------------------<BR>Raydar<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>From the Department of Redundancy Department.</FONT>||||reg||14
Z||000060||Fiero*101||12-08-2001||02:25 AM||||Speed Zone has to be the best ever Gone in 60 secs was GREAT dont get me wrong but the movie speed zone has the best start of any movie.<BR>All you hear is the roar of a the Lamborghini Countach and then it apears w/ cops chasing it of course and it comes to a dead end " or so it makes you think" they chase it a wile longer then you see this boy and his granpa trying to skip stones and this Lambo comes zooming across the lake like a bat out of hell!!!! that has to be the sweeeetest movie of all time  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>was it trick photography? or did they really jump that Lambo across that lake on to the other side ?<BR>any body know for sure?<P>just my 2 cents<P>Fiero*101<P>------------------<BR>Fiero*101<BR>Gold 86 SE 2M6<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mycar101.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000061||Oreif||12-08-2001||02:30 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Cliff Pennock:<BR><B>Can't remember the name but it was with Martin Sheen (when he was still young).</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>It was "The California Kid"<BR>He had a old Chevy rod and the sheriff would run Hot Rodders off a cliff. His brother was killed and he got revenge. <P>As for others I like: (in no particular order)<BR>Hollywood Knights<BR>American Grafitti<BR>Grand Theft Auto<BR>Days of Thunder<BR>Mad Max (gotta love the switchable blower)<BR>Dirty Mary Crazy Larry<BR>Gone in 60 seconds<BR>Vanishing Point<BR>The Smokey and the Bandit movie's<BR>Cannonball Run<BR>Deathrace 2000<BR>Hooper (The rocket car was cool)<BR>The Wraith<BR>Bulliit<BR>Christine<P><BR>Haven't seen Fast and Furious yet.<BR>Driven was OK<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 12-08-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000062||Gerald||12-09-2001||12:57 AM||||Wel I have watche alot of car movies but my favorites have to be, Ronin, The wraith ( I love daytonas and the turbo car was powered by a 2.2l tt 4 cyl built by dodge}, new gone in 60 seconds, f&f.||||reg||1
Z||000063||FieroMontreal||12-09-2001||01:39 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Fiero*101:<BR><B><P>was it trick photography? or did they really jump that Lambo across that lake on to the other side ?<BR>any body know for sure?<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>The pond was actually a flooded road.. all they did was make a little ramp to list the front wheels. There was only about 1' and maybe less of water on the road (where the lambo crosses the so called pond)...<P>Anyways.. Did you see the Fiero.. err.. Mera?<P>Did you notice the error with the Lambo in the Movie. They use 3 different lambos... well.. different edition Contachs! Look at the tail lamps and you will understand.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR><P>------------------<BR> -Alex <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigfieromontreal_1.gif">   <BR>1986 Fiero GT, STOCK Wingless, <BR>President of FieroMontreal... <A HREF="http://www.fieromontreal.com" TARGET=_blank>www.fieromontreal.com</A> <BR>and Regional Director of CFOG-I for Eastern Canada.||||reg||1
Z||000064||Oreif||12-09-2001||09:15 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FieroMontreal:<BR><B> The pond was actually a flooded road.. all they did was make a little ramp to list the front wheels. There was only about 1' and maybe less of water on the road (where the lambo crosses the so called pond)...<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I remember some show where they showed the stunt. It was a<BR>like above a flooded road with 1' of water. But to make the car "appear" to "skip" they had sheet metal plates mounted on the bottom so it would not slow the car down. The first time they did it the water killed the engine and dragged the car down. The entire bottom was flat.<BR><P>------------------<BR>             <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">           <BR><FONT SIZE="1"><B><I>Happiness isn't around the corner...<BR>Happiness IS the corner.</I></B></FONT>||||reg||1
